(END-TO-END MLOPS PROJECT REPORT) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(HEART DISEASE RISK CLASSIFICATION API) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Student: Santhosh Mohan) Tj T*
(BITS ID: 2025ae05426) Tj T*
(Repository: https://github.com/Explore-AI-Engg/MLOPS) Tj T*
(Dataset: UCI Cleveland Heart Disease dataset) Tj T*
(Project status: Local pipeline and GKE deployment verified; GitHub Actions success evidence) Tj T*
(is pending the next workflow run) Tj T*
() Tj T*
( This report is written from the implementation in this repository. The supplied reference) Tj T*
(report was used only to understand a possible academic report structure. Its wording,) Tj T*
(screenshots, code, and numerical results are not used here.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(ABSTRACT) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This project implements a reproducible machine-learning service for binary heart-disease) Tj T*
(risk classification. The solution begins with scripted acquisition of the UCI dataset,) Tj T*
(validates and transforms the data, compares Logistic Regression and Random Forest models,) Tj T*
(tracks experiments with MLflow, and persists the selected preprocessing-and-model pipeline) Tj T*
(as a Joblib artifact. A FastAPI service exposes health, prediction, and Prometheus metrics) Tj T*
(endpoints. Automated tests and linting run in GitHub Actions, while a Docker image packages) Tj T*
(the API and trained artifact for deployment to Google Kubernetes Engine \(GKE\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The project deliberately keeps preprocessing inside the persisted scikit-learn pipeline.) Tj T*
(This prevents training-serving skew: the same imputers, scaling rules, and categorical) Tj T*
(encoding learned during training are used for API requests. Operational logs exclude patient) Tj T*
(feature values and record only request metadata, status, and latency.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. PROJECT OBJECTIVE AND ARCHITECTURE) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The objective is to demonstrate the complete lifecycle rather than only achieve a high) Tj T*
(offline score:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. Acquire and validate data.) Tj T*
(2. Explore data quality, distributions, correlation, and class balance.) Tj T*
(3. Train at least two classifiers using a reproducible pipeline.) Tj T*
(4. Select a model using cross-validation and clinically relevant metrics.) Tj T*
(5. Track parameters, metrics, plots, and model artifacts.) Tj T*
(6. Test data processing, modeling, and API behavior.) Tj T*
(7. Package the service in Docker.) Tj T*
(8. Deploy the image to Kubernetes.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
