(9. Expose health, prediction, logs, and metrics for operation.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The logical flow is:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(text) Tj T*
(UCI dataset) Tj T*
(    - download_data.py) Tj T*
(    - prepare_data.py) Tj T*
(    - eda.py) Tj T*
(    - train.py + MLflow) Tj T*
(    - artifacts/model.joblib) Tj T*
(    - Docker image) Tj T*
(    - GHCR) Tj T*
(    - GKE Deployment) Tj T*
(    - LoadBalancer Service) Tj T*
(    - /health, /predict, /metrics) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The repository separates responsibilities:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(- app/: reusable application and preprocessing code.) Tj T*
(- scripts/: repeatable data, EDA, training, and smoke-test entry points.) Tj T*
(- tests/: automated tests.) Tj T*
(- artifacts/: persisted models and metadata.) Tj T*
(- outputs/eda/: generated visualizations.) Tj T*
(- deployment/: Kubernetes resources.) Tj T*
(- .github/workflows/: CI and deployment automation.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. DATA ACQUISITION AND PREPARATION) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The download script obtains the public UCI archive from the configured source URL and writes) Tj T*
(a validated raw CSV. The Cleveland dataset contains 303 observations and 13 predictor) Tj T*
(columns. The original target uses values from 0 to 4; this project maps 0 to no observed) Tj T*
(disease and values 1 through 4 to disease present.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The data preparation process:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. Checks the expected columns and row structure.) Tj T*
(2. Converts the target to a binary value.) Tj T*
(3. Represents missing values explicitly.) Tj T*
(4. Writes the processed CSV under data/processed/.) Tj T*
(5. Leaves the raw download available for reproducibility.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
